\q2 \rb and clouds|וְעָנָ֖ן\rb* \rb are the dust|אֲבַ֥ק\rb* \rb beneath His feet|רַגְלָֽיו׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 4 \rb He rebukes|גּוֹעֵ֤ר\rb* \rb the sea|בַּיָּם֙\rb* \rb and dries it up|וַֽיַּבְּשֵׁ֔הוּ\rb*;
\q2 \rb He makes all|וְכָל־\rb* \rb the rivers|הַנְּהָר֖וֹת\rb* \rb run dry|הֶֽחֱרִ֑יב\rb*.
\q1 \rb Bashan|בָּשָׁן֙\rb* \rb and Carmel|וְכַרְמֶ֔ל\rb* \rb wither|אֻמְלַ֤ל\rb*,
\q2 \rb and the flower|וּפֶ֥רַח\rb* \rb of Lebanon|לְבָנ֖וֹן\rb* \rb wilts|אֻמְלָֽל׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 5 \rb The mountains|הָרִים֙\rb* \rb quake|רָעֲשׁ֣וּ\rb* \rb before Him|מִמֶּ֔נּוּ\rb*,
\q2 \rb and the hills|וְהַגְּבָע֖וֹת\rb* \rb melt away|הִתְמֹגָ֑גוּ\rb*;
\q1 \rb the earth|הָאָ֙רֶץ֙\rb* \rb trembles|וַתִּשָּׂ֤א\rb* \rb at His presence|מִפָּנָ֔יו\rb*—
\q2 \rb the world|וְתֵבֵ֖ל\rb* \rb and all|וְכָל־\rb* \rb its dwellers|יֹ֥שְׁבֵי\rb*\rb |בָֽהּ׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 6 \rb Who|מִ֣י\rb* \rb can withstand|לִפְנֵ֤י\rb*\rb |יַֽעֲמ֔וֹד\rb* \rb His indignation|זַעְמוֹ֙\rb*?
\q2 \rb Who|וּמִ֥י\rb* \rb can endure|יָק֖וּם\rb* \rb His burning anger|בַּחֲר֣וֹן\rb*\rb |אַפּ֑וֹ\rb*?
\q1 \rb His wrath|חֲמָתוֹ֙\rb* \rb is poured out|נִתְּכָ֣ה\rb* \rb like fire|כָאֵ֔שׁ\rb*;
