\q2 \rb the valiant warriors|אַנְשֵׁי־\rb*\rb |חַ֙יִל֙\rb* \rb are dressed in scarlet|מְתֻלָּעִ֔ים\rb*.
\q1 \rb The fittings|פְּלָד֥וֹת\rb* \rb of the chariots|הָרֶ֖כֶב\rb* \rb flash like fire|בְּאֵשׁ־\rb*
\q2 \rb on the day|בְּי֣וֹם\rb* \rb they are prepared|הֲכִינ֑וֹ\rb*,
\q1 \rb and the spears of cypress|וְהַבְּרֹשִׁ֖ים\rb*
\q2 \rb have been brandished|הָרְעָֽלוּ׃\rb*.\f + \fr 2:3 \ft Hebrew; alternately, the spears may be of \fqa pine \ft or \fqa juniper \ft or \fqa fir\ft ; LXX and Syriac \fqa they are prepared, and the horsemen rush to and fro.\f*
\q1 \v 4 \rb The chariots|הָרֶ֔כֶב\rb* \rb dash|יִתְהוֹלְל֣וּ\rb* \rb through the streets|בַּֽחוּצוֹת֙\rb*;
