\q2 \rb and carried away|הֹֽעֲלָ֑תָה\rb*;
\q1 \rb her maidservants|וְאַמְהֹתֶ֗יהָ\rb* \rb moan|מְנַֽהֲגוֹת֙\rb* \rb like|כְּק֣וֹל\rb* \rb doves|יוֹנִ֔ים\rb*,
\q2 \rb and beat|מְתֹפְפֹ֖ת\rb* \rb upon|עַל־\rb* \rb their breasts|לִבְבֵהֶֽן׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 8 \rb Nineveh|וְנִינְוֵ֥ה\rb* \rb has been like a pool|כִבְרֵֽכַת־\rb* \rb of water|מַ֖יִם\rb*
\q2 \rb throughout|הִ֑יא\rb* \rb her days|מִ֣ימֵי\rb*,
\q2 \rb but now|וְהֵ֣מָּה\rb* \rb it is draining away|נָסִ֔ים\rb*.
\q1 “\rb Stop|עִמְד֥וּ\rb*! \rb Stop!” they cry|עֲמֹ֖דוּ\rb*,
\q2 \rb but no|וְאֵ֥ין\rb* \rb one turns back|מַפְנֶֽה׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 9 “\rb Plunder|בֹּ֥זּוּ\rb* \rb the silver|כֶ֖סֶף\rb*!
\q2 \rb Plunder|בֹּ֣זּוּ\rb* \rb the gold|זָהָ֑ב\rb*!”
\q1 \rb There is no|וְאֵ֥ין\rb* \rb end|קֵ֙צֶה֙\rb* \rb to the treasure|לַתְּכוּנָ֔ה\rb*,
\q2 \rb an abundance|כָּבֹ֕ד\rb* \rb of every|מִכֹּ֖ל\rb* \rb precious|חֶמְדָּֽה׃\rb* \rb thing|כְּלִ֥י\rb*.
\q1 \v 10 \rb She is emptied|בּוּקָ֥ה\rb*!
\q2 \rb Yes , she is desolate|וּמְבוּקָ֖ה\rb* \rb and laid waste|וּמְבֻלָּקָ֑ה\rb*!
\q1 \rb Hearts|וְלֵ֨ב\rb* \rb melt|נָמֵ֜ס\rb*, \rb knees|בִּרְכַּ֗יִם\rb* \rb knock|וּפִ֣ק\rb*,
\q2 \rb bodies|מָתְנַ֔יִם\rb* \rb tremble|וְחַלְחָלָה֙\rb*, \rb and every|בְּכָל־\rb* \rb face|וּפְנֵ֥י\rb*\rb |כֻלָּ֖ם\rb* \rb grows pale|קִבְּצ֥וּ\rb*\rb |פָארֽוּר׃\rb*!
\b 
\q1 \v 11 \rb Where|אַיֵּה֙\rb* \rb is the lions’|אֲרָי֔וֹת\rb* \rb lair|מְע֣וֹן\rb*
\q2 \rb or the feeding ground|וּמִרְעֶ֥ה\rb*\rb |ה֖וּא\rb* \rb of the young lions|לַכְּפִרִ֑ים\rb*,
\q1 \rb where|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb the lion|אַרְיֵ֨ה\rb* \rb and lioness|לָבִ֥יא\rb*\rb |שָׁ֛ם\rb* \rb prowled|הָלַךְ֩\rb* \rb with their|אַרְיֵ֖ה\rb* \rb cubs|גּ֥וּר\rb*,
\q2 \rb with nothing|וְאֵ֥ין\rb* \rb to frighten them away|מַחֲרִֽיד׃\rb*?
\q1 \v 12 \rb The lion|אַרְיֵ֤ה\rb* \rb mauled|טֹרֵף֙\rb* \rb enough for|בְּדֵ֣י\rb* \rb its cubs|גֹֽרוֹתָ֔יו\rb*
\q2 \rb and strangled prey|וּמְחַנֵּ֖ק\rb* \rb for the lioness|לְלִבְאֹתָ֑יו\rb*.
\q1 \rb It filled|וַיְמַלֵּא־\rb* \rb its dens|חֹרָ֔יו\rb* \rb with the kill|טֶ֣רֶף\rb*,
\q2 \rb and its lairs|וּמְעֹֽנֹתָ֖יו\rb* \rb with mauled prey|טְרֵפָֽה׃\rb*.
\b 
\q1 \v 13 “\rb Behold|הִנְנִ֣י\rb*, \rb I am against you|אֵלַ֗יִךְ\rb*,”
\q2 \rb declares|נְאֻם֙\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֣ה\rb* \rb of Hosts|צְבָא֔וֹת\rb*.
\q1 “\rb I will reduce|וְהִבְעַרְתִּ֤י\rb* \rb your chariots|רִכְבָּ֔הּ\rb* \rb to cinders|בֶֽעָשָׁן֙\rb*,
\q2 \rb and the sword|חָ֑רֶב\rb* \rb will devour|תֹּ֣אכַל\rb* \rb your young lions|וּכְפִירַ֖יִךְ\rb*.
\q1 \rb I will cut off|וְהִכְרַתִּ֤י\rb* \rb your prey|טַרְפֵּ֔ךְ\rb* \rb from the earth|מֵאֶ֙רֶץ֙\rb*,
\q2 \rb and the voices|ק֥וֹל\rb* \rb of your messengers|מַלְאָכֵֽכֵה׃ס\rb*
\q2 \rb will no longer|וְלֹֽא־\rb* \rb be heard|יִשָּׁמַ֥ע\rb*\rb |ע֖וֹד\rb*.”
\c 3
\s1 Judgment on Nineveh
